# TRIC coordinates on the Morse bulk cell. Bonds are the two nearest Cartesian neighbors. Distance coordinates are the library's Cartesian differences, so a minimum-image neighbor is not used: that pair can be a long Cartesian vector and does not describe the periodic contact. The covalent first shell is not used: its Wilson G matrix is about a tebibyte. A coordinate rebuild keeps that neighbor list. Atoms are Pt. The stop and trust settings match the Cartesian Morse row. A failed coordinate rebuild can continue in Cartesian coordinates.
